 "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 375853, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MG67pwd4YTMf1RV1N5d6kZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381384, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. Under that rule, `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I switched it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool returned \"Unknown advisory.\" The fix follows what the test and the docstring both say.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PV6uYD3yJhXS3K1Hp598dR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BBrcu1PFGDqx2xtnj6iCBT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016NbWf4UGM7twVnVGX7pac7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015RV3YWZHjZK4aiDUsizVwH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017a8sq2fjaeVsgfFLDqZ237", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0148RGEU2uen4YGm4J3qVYe2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Vg4pxE5uyHDnctyeESVa28", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MG67pwd4YTMf1RV1N5d6kZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring stating ROUND_HALF_EVEN per FIN-212).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. Under that rule, `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I switched it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool returned \"Unknown advisory.\" The fix follows what the test and the docstring both say.", "type": "text"}]}]}